<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Semarang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Semarang is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-java">Central Java</a> province, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, and a major port on the north coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>. Ceded by Mataram to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-east-india-company">Dutch East India Company</a> in the late 1670s in return for military help, it became the Company's main base on the north coast in the eighteenth century. It grew into an important colonial trading and railway centre with a large Chinese community.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/semarang.jpg" alt="Semarang" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uncredited · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lawang_Sewu_in_Semarang_City.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Rice, timber and other produce were still exported through Jepara and <b>Semarang</b>, increasingly to the Dutch at Batavia.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mataram-sultanate">Mataram Sultanate · Socioeconomy</a></li></ul></section>
